gnome-shell (50.1-0ubuntu1.5+piano5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * keyboard: ignore events without an actor in maybeHandleEvent(). Every
    touch release under a grab (lock screen, login screen, menus, modal
    dialogs) threw from keyboardBox.contains(); gnome-shell 51 removed the
    method. This replaces the piano-osk-guard extension, which the user's
    extension settings could turn off.
  * Map external touchscreens to the external monitor. While exactly one
    monitor other than the built-in panel is connected, every USB or
    Bluetooth touchscreen gets it as its configured output, as Android does,
    instead of Mutter's built-in panel fallback. This replaces the
    piano-touch-output extension and also runs on the login and lock
    screens, whatever the user's extension settings.

