gnome-shell (50.1-0ubuntu1.5+piano4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * brightnessManager: save and restore the monitor brightnesses
    (upstream 29c61c40, MR !4006). The slider is no longer re-read from the
    backlight at every login, so automatic brightness no longer drifts by
    the difference between its target and the middle of the slider. The
    color mode field of the saved monitor key stays empty: mutter 50 has no
    meta_monitor_get_color_mode_string().
  * brightnessManager: when automatic brightness takes over a monitor that
    has no saved value and that the user has not adjusted, start its slider
    at the neutral middle instead of the backlight level it found, so the
    first session after an upgrade does not keep that level as an offset.
    A slider still taken from the backlight is not saved, so a first session
    without automatic brightness does not leave that offset behind either.
    The login screen follows the backlight it finds, as in 50.x, and saves
    nothing.
  * brightnessManager: store the vendor, product and serial that a panel
    without an EDID does not have as empty strings, so that its brightness
    can be saved at all.
  * shellDBus: reply to Lock when the lock screen is already shown
    (upstream 671460fa, MR !4511), so that gnome-settings-daemon does not
    block for the D-Bus timeout when the lid closes on a locked screen.
  * screenShield: finish the lock when preparing for sleep. A lock whose
    fade user input cancelled stayed locked but never became active, so
    its sleep inhibitor held every suspend until logind's timeout with the
    screen dark and the lid and power button ignored. The inhibitor now
    follows ubuntu-lock-on-suspend only, the setting that makes the shell
    lock for sleep.

